+-Local changes:
++Official presentation adopted on 2026-10-22:
+ 
+-- Preserve the standalone controlled component, entries, status, summary, live region, latest activity, and outside attention/final slots. Homer supplies original ordered entries and lifecycle; no tool execution or state classification is added here.
+-- Replace upstream Base UI collapsible neighbor with installed `@radix-ui/react-collapsible@1.2.1`. Replace Tailwind, `cn`, and `collapsePanel` with ordinary Homer CSS. No Base UI, Tailwind, surfaces package, theme initialization, or dependency upgrade.
+-- Replace the single lucide chevron with its equivalent inline SVG. No lucide dependency.
+-- Add typed trigger/content props for caller-owned focus refs and mounted-hidden content, `aria-busy`, and whitespace between the status and duration. CSS retains Homer spacing, focus treatment, narrow layouts, and reduced motion.
++- Preserve upstream markup, utility class strings, 12px root/list gaps, 14px type and chevron, 6px trigger gap/radius, 4px trigger padding, start-aligned tabular summary, 1px list rule with 6px start margin / 14px padding / 8px top padding, latest activity, status-only empty row and outside attention/final slots. No Homer header rule, full-width trigger, reduced font or second tool disclosure.
++- `run-activity.css` provides exact component-scoped equivalents of those utilities. Bind upstream muted-foreground/foreground/border/ring roles to existing Homer variables locally. No global theme, Tailwind reset, shadcn initialization or dependency/runtime update. Font family inherits the host, as upstream does.
++- Keep installed `@radix-ui/react-collapsible@1.2.1` instead of adding Base UI. Its measured height and Presence lifecycle implement upstream `collapsePanel`'s 200ms cubic-bezier(0.32,0.72,0,1) expansion/collapse using scoped keyframes; reduced motion is immediate. No caller forceMount/hidden override. The chevron's geometry is the upstream lucide ChevronRight rendered inline, without a package install.
++- Add typed trigger/content props solely for existing focus refs and title; keep official styles. Homer owns persisted run identity, original event order, actual timing, lifecycle and terminal-once collapse, including the existing running-default-open contract. These are adapter behavior, not capabilities of the official component. Streaming and explicit expansion remain stable.
++- Public commentary and each tool fact are supplied as ordinary entries. Original IDs/revisions/order and exact task/version/Run remain owned by existing projection. No raw tool arguments/results or model internals enter the UI. Returned calls are not passed checks. Independent Workers, important exceptions, valid pending decisions and formal answers/files retain their existing positions and contracts.
+ 
+ Direct dependencies also declared by this change: existing `@assistant-ui/core@0.3.30` (MIT, public `@assistant-ui/core/react` copy hook), existing `@radix-ui/react-focus-scope@1.3.1` (MIT, WorkOS; task dialog focus loop). No new installed packages or transitive lock entries. The copy hook uses a Homer writer for pending/error feedback and one synchronous clipboard initiation; it does not use the Copy primitive, whose installed API cannot supply this writer.
+ 
+ The installed Attachment primitives/adapter own the draft attachment collection. Homer retains the upload/discard transport, stable request/upload identity, confirmed asset metadata, batch validation, and running-send/IME form adapter. `unstable_Thumb` in this installed version has no image URL lifecycle; the small per-row object URL effect, keyed by the original attachment ID, supplies the existing local preview.
+ 
